# Final product principle

> **The Cockpit should never make the user choose between simplicity, power, and truth. It should present the smallest truthful surface needed for the current decision, preserve the full governed system underneath, reveal deeper control exactly when context makes it useful, never confuse activity with externally verified and settled outcomes, and treat every report as a reviewable lens over canonical evidence—not as a prettier substitute for truth.**

